-- Fetch-stage events, relative to the fetcher's scope (TOP.NzeaCore.core.front.ifu).
--
-- Bind them to compose with other scopes, e.g. an instruction stream against the retire events in core.pulse:
--   pulse property --event nzea_core/fetch.pulse <IFU> Fetch --event nzea_core/core.pulse <MIDDLE> Core \
--       --eval 'Core.redirect --40 Fetch.i_fetch'

-- A fetch request the bus accepted: this is the cycle the pc advances on.
i_fetch = ibus_req_valid && ibus_req_ready

-- The bus answered, whatever the response's epoch: a killed stream is digested, not refused.
i_resp = ibus_resp_valid

-- A request is waiting for the bus. Stuck high is a fetch deadlock (the ready side never comes); on this bus it is
-- also the signature of the one-slot bridge, which refuses a new request exactly in the cycle it presents the previous
-- response, so `i_stall` counts the same cycles as `i_resp`.
i_stall = ibus_req_valid && !ibus_req_ready

-- A fetched word the register between fetch and decode took, which is what carries the stream forward.
out_fire = out_valid && out_ready
